xjq: the empty string keeps an empty text node (checkpoint 3)

Sentence: "Primitive values map to element text: booleans as `true`/`false`, numbers as
minimal string form, null as empty." It says what null becomes and nothing about `""`. Both
min12-ABDFJKMN runs on v1 guarded the text assignment with `if text:`, so `{"key": ""}`
serialized as `<key type="str"/>`; the hidden test wants `<key type="str"></key>` and the
reference solution assigns the converted text unconditionally (lxml then writes the open-close
form for `""` and for null alike). Test: test_json_empty_string_preserves_element_with_empty_text
(checkpoint 3, carried to 5; the one miss left on v1, 166/167 twice).

--- a/xjq/checkpoint_3.md
+++ b/xjq/checkpoint_3.md
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
